_score_roic_consistency":20.8,"_gate_incr_roic":0.16211861734201713,"_gp_incr_roic":true,"_score_incr_roic":70.7,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":0.0,"_gate_pool_share":-0.20889111997714171,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":0.0,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":0.07557296732110652,"_gp_fcf_durability":true,"_score_fcf_durability":62.8,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.08220076796620963,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":100.0,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.005539204288676047,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":56.9,"_gate_sbc_dilution":null,"_gp_sbc_dilution":null,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":1.0000001e-05,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":0.0,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Sanofi engages in the research, development, manufacture, and marketing of therapeutic solutions in Finland and Germany. It provides immunology and inflammation, rare diseases neurology, oncology, and other vaccines. It also offers poliomyelitis, pertussis, and haemophilus influenzae type b (Hib) pediatric vaccines; respiratory syncytial virus protection; hexavalent combination vaccines that includes hepatitis A, typhoid, yellow fever, and rabies vaccines; and Fluzone, a flu vaccine. It has a collaboration and license agreement with Exscientia to develop small-molecule for oncology and immunology; ABL Bio, Inc. to develop ABL301 for treatment of alpha-synucleinopathies; and Innate Pharma SA for cell engager program targeting B7-H3. Further, it has a collaboration agreements with Atomwise to use ATOMNET platform and Insilico Medicine to use Pharma.AI, a medicine's AI platform; Kymera Therapeutics, Inc. to develop and commercialize protein degrader therapies targeting IRAK4 in patients with immune-inflammatory diseases; Nurix Therapeutics, Inc. to develop protein degradation therapies; Denali Therapeutics Inc. to treat systemic inflammatory diseases, such as ulcerative colitis; and Adagene Inc. for development of antibody-based therapies. Additionally, it has a collaboration with Scribe Therapeutics Inc. to develop genome editing technologies; Teva Pharmaceuticals to co-develop and co-commercialize TEV'574, for treatment of ulcerative colitis and Crohn's disease; co-promotion service agreement with Provention Bio, Inc. for the commercialization of teplizumab; and antibody collaboration with Regeneron Pharmaceuticals, Inc. to develop antibodies, such as Dupixent (dupilumab) as treatment for diseases driven by type 2 inflammation. The company was formerly known as Sanofi-Aventis and changed its name to Sanofi in May 2011. Sanofi was incorporated in 1994 and is headquartered in Paris, France.","ceo_bio":"Ms. Belen  Garijo Lopez M.D. | CEO & Director | Age 65","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 74K people. Each employee generates $130K of free cash flow annually.","financial_summary":["Sanofi is a large-cap healthcare business with a $128.1B market cap.","Returns on capital run at 8% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $9.8B in free cash flow, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.37\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.9\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 11.3\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 8.2% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.5) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Payout ratio looks stretched \u2014 the dividend\u2019s own margin of safety is thin","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.43553559974342876},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 57% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Valued at a 39% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Large open-market insider purchases (net $5.1M) \u2014 management putting its own capital behind the business","23 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 13% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (25.6% return)"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Sanofi (SNY) Added for High Cash Flow Yield and Pipeline Rebuilding","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/sanofi-sny-added-high-cash-145952602.html","date":"2026-11-27","timestamp":1795791592.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.902,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"SNY Up Almost 29% in a Month: Should You Buy, Hold or Sell the Stock?","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3036368/sny-up-almost-29-in-a-month-should-you-buy-hold-or-sell-the-stock?cid=CS-ZC-FT-analyst_blog%7Crank_focused-3036368","date":"2026-11-27","timestamp":1795781160.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Stocktwits Biotech Dealmaker: Sanofi\u2019s $41B Insmed Buyout Anchors Holiday Week As Lilly Continues Buying Spree","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/healthcare/articles/stocktwits-biotech-dealmaker-sanofi-41b-001023937.html","date":"2026-11-28","timestamp":1795824623.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.625,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":["m_and_a"]},{"title":"Sanofi Stock Surges 26% as $41 Billion Insmed Deal Boosts Confidence","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/sanofi-stock-surges-26-41-113324950.html","date":"2026-11-27","timestamp":1795779204.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.784,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Sanofi CEO got to work on $41 billion Insmed deal straight after taking office","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/sanofi-ceo-got-41-billion-060244000.html","date":"2026-11-27","timestamp":1795759937.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.226,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":["leadership"]},{"title":"Insmed's Sales Gave Notice A Year Early. Why Didn't The Stock?","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/insmeds-sales-gave-notice-early-144735365.html","date":"2026-11-27","timestamp":1795790855.0,"origi